---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Cupping Therapy | Nikki Leonardi Bodywork Traverse City" description="Cupping therapy for myofascial release and chronic tension. Suction-based work that does what pressure alone cannot. Traverse City, MI.">
  <div class="pt-16">
    <section class="py-24 px-6 bg-[#162040]">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <p class="section-label mb-4">Cupping Therapy</p>
        <h1 class="font-['Playfair_Display'] text-5xl text-[#f0f4ff] leading-tight mb-6">Cupping does something<br/>most hands can't —<br/><em class="text-[#c8a84b]">it lifts.</em></h1>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="py-20 px-6 bg-[#0d1428]">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-[#c8a84b]/70 leading-relaxed text-lg">
        <p>Most bodywork applies pressure down into the tissue. Cupping works the opposite way — it uses suction to lift the tissue, creating space and drawing circulation into areas that have been compressed or restricted.</p>
        <p>For myofascial work and chronic tension, that difference matters. Cupping reaches adhesions and restrictions that compression techniques simply can't access.</p>
        <p class="font-['Playfair_Display'] text-xl text-[#f0f4ff] italic">"My favorite is the cupping — it really releases the sticky myofascial connective tissue and promotes healing. I have felt mass improvement after this procedure."</p>
        <p class="text-[#c8a84b]/40 text-sm">— Michelle Mitchell</p>
        <p class="text-[#c8a84b]/50 text-sm pt-4">Cupping is typically incorporated within a broader integrative session rather than booked as a standalone service. Book a customized session and communicate your interest in cupping — Nikki will incorporate it where appropriate.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-12">
        <a href="/book" class="btn-primary">Book a Session</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
